Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: Advertise Mali-G78 support

Mali-G78 is a Valhall v9 GPU, similar enough to G57 to work without changes.
Tested on Google Tensor (gs101) in a Pixel 6, which contains Mali-G78 MP20
r0p1 (shader_present=0x779fff).

The kernel reports GPU_PROD_ID 0x9202. Decoded with the field macros in
pan_model.h that is arch_major 9, arch_minor 2, product_major 2, giving
PAN_PROD_ID(9, 2, 2). The same decoding reproduces the existing G57 entries
from their kernel IDs 0x9001 and 0x9003, and matches G68 at (9, 2, 4), which
is the same Valhall v9 family and differs only in product_major.

Tile buffer sizes and rates are taken from G57, as was done for G68.
TBOx is the performance counter set for this GPU (src/panfrost/perf/G78.xml).

--- a/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c
@@ -78,6 +78,8 @@
                                               MODEL_RATES(2, 4,  32)),
    VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(9, 0, 3), 0, "G57",    "TNAx", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(16384,  8192),
                                               MODEL_RATES(2, 4,  32)),
+   VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(9, 2, 2), 0, "G78",    "TBOx", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(16384,  8192),
+                                              MODEL_RATES(2, 4,  32)),
    VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(10, 8, 7), 0, "G610",   "TVIx", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(32768, 16384),
                                               MODEL_RATES(4, 8,  64)),
    VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(10, 12, 4), 0, "G310v1",   "TVAx", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(16384,  8192),
